invariant: INV-16
file: sha256.h
catches: hash_runtime_test
reason: sha256.h's sha256_on_instructions answers yes for a value without
  CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_SHA256, so a session whose caller never stated the
  timing of the SHA-256 instructions hashes its transcript and derives its
  keys on them, and on a CPU without them it dies of SIGILL at its first
  message (docs/decisions.md 93). The two paths compute the same bytes, so
  no vector can tell. bin/hash_runtime_test counts the calls into each
  path under every ch_cfg.cpu value and runs both on sha256.c's code, so
  its verdict is the same on every CPU.

--- old
    return (cpu & CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_SHA256) != 0;
--- new
    return (cpu & CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_SHA256) == 0;
